Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:57:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 0/7] media: i2c: ov7251: fixes and IR strobe support for Surface Book 2

The Microsoft Surface Book 2 has an OV7251 IR camera (Windows Hello)
next to its front camera, on the IPU3 CIO2. Its 850 nm emitter is wired
to the sensor's STROBE pin: ACPI describes no LED, GPIO or regulator for
it. With the mainline driver the camera streams, but always unlit.

Patches 1 to 5 fix issues found while testing the driver on this
machine:

- 1: the link frequency index is taken from the firmware list instead
  of the driver's table, so the sensor runs at 240 MHz while the
  firmware asks for 319.2 MHz (Fixes, Cc stable).
- 2: Daniel Scally's patch switching the gain control to
  V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN, carried by linux-surface.
- 3: control events, the one v4l2-compliance failure on the subdev.
- 4: the 60 and 90 fps frame intervals are accepted but the sensor
  keeps streaming at 30 fps, because the VBLANK control is not updated
  and rewrites the 30 fps frame length at stream start.
- 5: orientation and rotation controls from firmware.

Patches 6 and 7 add the emitter: 6 moves the strobe registers, which
the three mode tables write identically, out of the tables without
functional change, and 7 adds a V4L2_CID_FLASH_STROBE_OE control that
enables the STROBE pad, strobes every frame and makes the pulse follow
the exposure, from 52 lines up to 45% of the frame. The Windows driver
on this hardware clamps it to 52 to 776 lines, 45% of the 30 fps frame.

Measurements on a Surface Book 2 (i7-8650U), linux-surface 6.18.8 with
patches 1 and 3 to 6 built out of tree (2 was already applied):

- link frequency 319200000, pixel rate 63840000, 30.01 fps unchanged
- v4l2-compliance -u on the sensor subdev: 0 failures (was 1)
- --set-subdev-fps 60 / 90: 60.15 / 90.45 fps measured (was 30.01)
- orientation front, rotation 0
- dark frames and the sensor test pattern unchanged after patch 6
- 10 unbind/unload/load cycles: no warning in the kernel log

The strobe itself was verified with register writes on the stock
driver: 0x3005 = 0x08 and 0x3b81 = 0xff while streaming raise the mean
pixel value of an indoor IR frame from 20 to 103 (exposure 1704,
analogue gain 128). Patch 7 was build tested against 7.2 and 7.3-rc1
(W=1, checkpatch --strict) but has not run on hardware yet, since
V4L2_CID_FLASH_STROBE_OE is not in 6.18.

Antoine Pichot (6):
  media: i2c: ov7251: Fix link frequency index
  media: i2c: ov7251: Add control event support
  media: i2c: ov7251: Reset vblank when the frame interval changes
  media: i2c: ov7251: Add orientation and rotation controls
  media: i2c: ov7251: Move the strobe registers out of the mode tables
  media: i2c: ov7251: Add strobe output enable control

Daniel Scally (1):
  media: i2c: Clarify that gain is Analogue gain in OV7251

